What is AuthService?
This class is the front door to the entire backend. It handles identity, security checks, and user lifecycle events before anyone gets access to the rest of the system.

Instead of stuffing everything into controllers, AuthService keeps the core business logic clean by focusing on three main jobs:

User Registration (register)

Checks that the email isn't already taken in the database.

Hashes the raw password with BCrypt (salting happens automatically here).

Generates a secure activation token that expires in 24 hours.

Saves the new user with isEmailVerified = false.

Sends out a confirmation email via EmailService.

Returns basic user details without issuing a JWT yet (since they aren't verified).

Account Activation (verifyEmail)

Takes the token from the email link.

Checks if the token exists and makes sure the 24-hour window hasn't expired.

Flips isEmailVerified to true.

Clears the token fields from the database so the link cannot be used twice.

User Login (login)

Hands credentials over to Spring Security's AuthenticationManager.

Checks account status: if the email isn't verified or the account is marked INACTIVE, login is denied immediately.

If credentials and status are valid, it creates and returns a signed JWT Bearer token with the user's role and details.

What Does This File Call / Depend On?
Internal Services & Repositories
UserRepository: Talks to PostgreSQL. Checks for existing emails (existsByEmail), finds users by token (findByVerificationToken), and saves updated records (save).

JwtUtils: Creates signed JWT Bearer tokens containing the user's email and role.

EmailService: Sends out the verification link through SMTP (Gmail).

Spring Security Framework Tools
PasswordEncoder: Uses BCrypt to hash passwords before they touch the database.

AuthenticationManager: Spring Security's engine that checks if the entered password matches the stored hash and confirms the user is enabled.

Entities & Enums
User: The database entity representing the user account row.

UserStatus: Tracks whether the account is ACTIVE or INACTIVE (for soft deletion).

Role: Assigns system permissions (ROLE_ATTORNEY, ROLE_ADMIN, ROLE_FORENSIC_EXAMINER, ROLE_CLIENT).

Data Transfer Objects (DTOs)
RegisterRequest: Inbound JSON payload containing full name, email, password, and requested role.

LoginRequest: Inbound JSON payload containing email and password.

AuthResponse: Outbound response sent back to Postman or the frontend with user info and token details.

Custom Exceptions
BadRequestException: Thrown when an email already exists or a verification link is invalid/expired (returns HTTP 400).

ResourceNotFoundException: Safety check thrown if the logged-in user cannot be found in the database (returns HTTP 404).

